module gunbc.plans.dag_v2_defork_audit

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetirement, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock, TableBlock, AlignNone, ThematicBreak }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h2, h3, p, li, ul, ol, cell, row }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn dag_v2_defork_audit_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Audit/design authority, not a task ledger. One concept has one home; mechanical mirrors, identity forks and distinct concepts require different cuts. Current census comes from gunbc.defork_type_name_census; dated symbol/importer tables and correction receipts remain in [Original analysis and receipts](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/06d3c1c3149a7420c4a548b9aba9b15c721c635d/dag/gunbc/plans/dag_v2_defork_audit.dag). DESIGN and the cited carriers govern implementation."),
    h2(text: "Cross-tree admission and migration rule"),
    p(text: "Cross-tree ingest is live in both directions (#5473/#5486). The old fundamentality rank was deleted by #15080 under cross_tree_admission_is_namespace_membership (2026-10-25): gunbc.source_layout_namespaces owns namespace membership; namespace_declared checks storage admission before reading, and name_resolve admit_import_cross_tree_gate → cross_tree_edge_decision checks active-root admission. Undeclared namespaces refuse CrossTreeNamespaceUndeclared. long/cross_tree_real_ingest_activation reverses both tags as its control. repo_relative_dag_path fixed the absolute/relative seam (#5504); probe_selector_compute_fabric Optional/Option collision was resolved by a thin connector (#5904). Do not resurrect directional import barriers."),
    p(text: "A mechanical mirror cut deletes the copy, repoints consumers and preserves exact structural cardinality plus the original executing witnesses. A basename or zero shared-symbol count cannot establish distinct concepts. The type-name wall compares shared unqualified names with structural inequality; an empty intersection can make a guard vacuous. A closure count is not a task count or an authority ratchet."),
    h2(text: "Coercion: the measured correction governs"),
    p(text: "The original not-a-fork classification is retracted. std.coercion.dag_can_cast uses dag_cast_rules + grounded_primitive_coproduct_identities keyed by type-name strings and executes in v1.compiler.infer at kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch_bounded, application_type_names_compatible and validate_cast. v2.std.coercion.coercion_fold asks v2.std.find_witness.find_witness over node identity and has no established executing consumer. Both answer whether a value crosses models, with incompatible key relations and no conversion. A fixture must author its subject twice: that is evidence of the fork, filed as two_admission_authorities_keyed_on_different_relations, not fixture awkwardness."),
    p(text: "Seven supplied pairs demonstrate admission differences in both directions. Name-only: Int→Float and Int→Nat; Bool→Int was withdrawn by #12227 and remains a refusal control. Homomorphism-only: String→String, because preservation_rule_exact_structural_equality_zip_fold can express only identity. This raw-helper omission is not a production String identity refusal: live v1 compositions admit identity first. Each side matches its own contract. Repair remains deferred by the 2026-09-22 ruling, but is an admission-key replacement migration, not the formerly priced basename rename."),
    p(text: "v2.test.claim.coercion.two_algebra_fork pins the independent contracts with name_keyed_coercion_matches_the_declared_cast_rosters_holds, homomorphism_coercion_matches_the_structural_preservation_contract_holds and homomorphism_coercion_admits_only_identity_quality_holds. Adding Bool→Float reds only the roster claim; weakening structural preservation reds only the homomorphism claims. No extra cross-comparison claim: agreement is derived from the independently expected columns, and an entailed RED is not independently authorable."),
    h2(text: "Bindings: a scoped negative with an unresolved duplicate rule"),
    p(text: "std.occurrence_binding.occurrence_binding_from_candidates and v2.std.symbol_index.symbol_index_lexical_selection each match none/one/many over supplied empty, singleton, two-distinct, duplicate and three-element populations. This is not agreement by construction: neither contract decides list multiplicity versus DISTINCT candidate cardinality. Both currently treat a duplicate as two candidates by omission. Declare that rule on its owning carrier; keep the duplicate control enrolled."),
    p(text: "Production-site agreement is unmeasured: no v2 site calls the std fold, and std staged adoption excludes LexicalLookup because it lacks exact reference-occurrence Node/containment identity. Candidate producers are legitimately different layers, not compared. the_real_chain_walk_emits_the_population_the_fixtures_supply_holds pairs the supplied boundary with the real symbol_index_lexical_collect walk. Collapsing std to FoldOne reds only std; making v2 return Ambiguous on empty reds only v2. No redundant comparison claim."),
    h2(text: "Grounding decisions and residuals"),
    p(text: "The grounding cluster requires a design, not seven renames: algebra includes model/realization reflection and numeric completion; logic still needs the distinction between classical operations and grounded Bool decided; integer operations sit on the common width tower; float separates algebraic and bit-level operations. EffectShape differs by operation axis versus idempotency axis: decide whether these are orthogonal dimensions of one authority. TestClaim differs between proposition record and anchored assertion coproduct, entangled with numeric grounding, Value::Null and the generated test oracle. The original table records unique contributions. These are operator-designed grounding cuts, never mechanical repoints. Nat is resolved (2026-09-30): std.nat owns the Peano coproduct, gunbc.structural_realization_bindings.kernel_grounding_rows realizes it as kernel integer, std.magnitude is deleted, and v2.std.nat retains the node-bound law roster."),
    p(text: "Operator algebra authority is the structural FreeMonoid coproduct Empty | Cons; record methods derive from inhabitance. Do not revive RustCorpusRepr/HostNative/FaithfulFreeMonoid emitter mechanisms: those were deleted, and their old Root-A proposals are historical quarry. #5552 enabled generic-alias instantiation; recursive Cons.tail matching still needs its named resolver/infer judgment (the captured failure was variant not found: FreeMonoid). Escalate changes to those load-bearing layers under a current brief, not an old migration instruction. #6341 retired variant shadow roots and repointed consumers; remaining record-method divergence is a separate obligation."),
    p(text: "algebra-grounding-unification-design §9 separates reserved builtin free functions (filter, length, any, contains, skip, is_empty, non_empty, bag_eq: dissolve to methods, not nicknames), emitter realization debt, and QualifiedName ownership. Historic hardcoded v2_std_algebra helpers and one-way-tree prerequisites cannot be treated as current instructions after their mechanisms were deleted. Definition unification follows the generic-alias keystone: make coproduct authority singular and derive record methods from inhabitance, then repoint consumers. String = FreeMonoid<Char>, List<T> = FreeMonoid<T> and QualifiedName = FreeMonoid<Symbol> remain the intended aliases; obsolete host-emitter mechanisms supply no implementation authority. The self_gen8 ignored cases move from stays_unemitted to grounded List<T>=Vec<T> expectations with that unification. Structural unification does not discharge divergent record methods; activate the flag-ANY wall only when its grounded subject and actual mismatches are resolved."),
    p(text: "dag/std/node.dag is the live v1-only inductive-field authority (compiler_inductive_fields/compiler_recursive_types/is_compiler_recursive_type); it is not an imposter. On v1 deletion it becomes dead and is deleted, ending the basename collision without a rename. Stage all rename/repoint files atomically: a frozen merge SHA captured mid-change stays inconsistent; rerunning that same SHA cannot repair it."),
  ]
}

data dag_v2_defork_audit_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "dag-v2-defork-audit",
  title: "Plan — De-fork `dag/` ↔ `src/v2/` (collapse the duplicated standard library)",
  body: dag_v2_defork_audit_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this doc when the fork census reaches zero — when no `std` basename denotes two concepts and every concept has a single authority. The census now has **three categories**, dissolving on different triggers: **(a) True mirrors** (`reducible`, `measure`) — mechanical collapse; dissolve into their carriers (absent files, re-pointed imports) as each PR lands. Plus `probe_selector` (the step-4 data-import unblock), independent. **(b) Grounding divergences** (`algebra`, `logic`, `nat`, `integer`, `float`, `effects`, `verification`) — downstream of the operator's grounding-unification design; tracked here as decision-input until that design lands and the repoints become mechanical. **(c) v1-artifact collisions** (`node`, `coercion`) — deferred to v1-shrink; trigger \"when v1's consumers of `dag/std/\{node,coercion\}` are removed\" (`node` self-dissolves, `coercion` shrinks to a v1-free rename). At the point all three are resolved the carriers tell the whole story and this audit is redundant.")
  }
}
